.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-vm-snapshot-rollback - Roll a VM back to its newest snapshot, then prove the guest is running


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge vm snapshot rollback <target-id> <vmid> <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Roll a VM back to a snapshot, then prove the rolled-back guest is running.

.PP
Only the NEWEST snapshot can be rolled back to: if newer snapshots exist,
the rollback is refused before anything is sent, and the refusal names them
and the vm snapshot delete command that would discard them. Rollback never
deletes a snapshot itself.

.PP
After the rollback, a witness command is run in the guest through the QEMU
guest agent: by default /bin/echo with a fresh random marker, which assumes
a POSIX guest. --witness-command (repeatable: one argument each) and
--witness-marker replace it, for example for a Windows guest. The witness
waits up to --witness-timeout for the agent. --no-witness skips it.

.PP
Output: target, vmid, snapshot, rollback=completed and witness=verified (or
witness=skipped). If the witness fails, the command exits 1 and says that
the rollback itself completed but could not be proven.

.PP
Locking: the VM's pveforge lock is held for the whole command (a shared
read lock for list). It serialises pveforge processes only: a change made
at the same time from PVE's web UI or qm is not held off.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rollback

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB--no-witness\fP[=false]
	do not run the witness command after the rollback

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--witness-command\fP=[]
	the witness command to run in the guest, one argument per flag (needs --witness-marker)

.PP
\fB--witness-marker\fP=""
	text the witness command's output must contain

.PP
\fB--witness-timeout\fP=2m0s
	how long the witness may wait for the guest agent (at most 30m0s)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-vm-snapshot(1)\fP
